<section aria-labelledby="demo-h">
  <h2 id="demo-h" class="type-h2">List row</h2>
  <p>The whole row is the link. On hover the row fills with the blue tint, the title underline goes to 2px, and the arrow moves 4px to the right. Pressed uses a deeper tint. The focus ring wraps the row. Rows have an arrow and no button, so they need that clear hover state.</p>
  {% demo "Two list rows and a locked row", "block" %}
  <section class="cs-more" aria-labelledby="more-demo-h">
    <h3 class="cs-more__heading type-subhead" id="more-demo-h">More work</h3>
    <ul class="cs-more__list" role="list">
      <li>
        <a class="cs-row-link" href="#">
          <span class="cs-row-link__text">
            <span class="cs-row-link__title type-h3">Case study title</span>
            <span class="cs-row-link__category type-label">Category</span>
          </span>
          <span class="cs-row-link__arrow" aria-hidden="true">{% icon "arrow_forward" %}</span>
        </a>
      </li>
      <li>
        <a class="cs-row-link" href="#">
          <span class="cs-row-link__text">
            <span class="cs-row-link__title type-h3">Another case study title</span>
            <span class="cs-row-link__category type-label">Category</span>
          </span>
          <span class="cs-row-link__arrow" aria-hidden="true">{% icon "arrow_forward" %}</span>
        </a>
      </li>
      <li>
        <a class="cs-row-link cs-row-link--locked" href="#">
          <span class="cs-row-link__text">
            <span class="cs-row-link__title type-h3">Locked case study title</span>
            <span class="cs-row-link__category type-label">Category</span>
          </span>
          <span class="cs-row-link__arrow" aria-hidden="true">{% icon "lock" %}</span>
          <span class="cs-row-link__helper type-small">Password required.</span>
        </a>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>
  {% enddemo %}
  <p>A locked row looks like the others, with a lock in place of the arrow and a small helper line, here "Password required.", under it. The lock does not move on hover. The row is taller because of the helper line. Its heights are in the last sentence of the Tablet section below, and the other widths are on the <a href="/components/more-case-studies/">More case studies</a> page.</p>
</section>
<section aria-labelledby="tablet-h">
  <h2 id="tablet-h" class="type-h2">Tablet</h2>
  <p>From 768 to 1023px the row sits on the 8-column grid with 16px gutters and is 736px wide with its 16px side padding. The title takes columns 1 to 4, the category columns 5 and 6, and the arrow cell columns 7 and 8, right-aligned. An unlocked row is 112px tall. The frame below is 768px wide, so it shows the tablet layout on any screen.</p>
  <figure class="preview-frame">
    <div class="preview-frame__scroller" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="List row at tablet width, scrollable">
      <iframe src="/previews/list-row/" width="768" height="468" title="List row at tablet width" loading="lazy"></iframe>
    </div>
    <figcaption class="preview-frame__caption type-small">Two rows and a locked row at 768px. Hover and focus work in the frame.</figcaption>
  </figure>
  <p>In a locked row the lock takes the arrow's place and the helper line sits under it in columns 7 and 8, where a longer line wraps to two. The title and category are centered against both. The row's height follows the helper line: 152px when it wraps to two lines, as "Password required. Email me for access." does, and 132px when it fits on one line, as it does in the frame above.</p>
</section>
<section aria-labelledby="desktop-h">
  <h2 id="desktop-h" class="type-h2">Desktop</h2>
  <p>The desktop layout starts at 1024px. The frame below is 1280px wide, so it shows the desktop row on any screen. In the locked row the helper line sits under the lock.</p>
  <figure class="preview-frame">
    <div class="preview-frame__scroller" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="List row at desktop width, scrollable">
